." mdview manual page for macOS
.TH MDVIEW 1 "2025-12-09" "mdview 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdview \- render Markdown in the terminal with less-like navigation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdview
.RI [ \-h ]
.RI [ \-\-pager
.I COMMAND
.RI ]
.RI [ \-V ]
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
mdview renders Markdown and plain text with ANSI styling and pipes the output
to pagers such as
.BR less (1)
for comfortable navigation. The program falls back to standard-library paging
when Rich or a pager is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B path
Path to a Markdown or text file to view.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-pager " " COMMAND
Optional pager command to override the default less/pydoc pager (for example,
.BR "less \-R" ).
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the mdview version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B posix/mdview-help.txt
The shared POSIX help text derived from the argparse configuration. Keep this
file in sync with the parser when packaging the macOS man page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR pydoc (1)
